  "body": "Auction: 8-12 The Promenade, Takapuna on Thursday 17 December 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nSolid, sunny, and surprisingly spacious, this Cheltenham home is a rare find.\r\n\r\nWith a floor area of 90m², this end unit is considerably larger than your usual brick-and-tile home. Built in the 1960s, it sits in a beautiful garden bordering the cricket reserve, combining solid construction, sunshine, and a wonderful Cheltenham location.\r\n\r\nA warm sunroom welcomes you in and offers a lovely spot for morning coffee. As you enter the good-sized lounge, you will find an abundance of natural light and far-reaching views. The kitchen adjoins an additional dining area, where plantation shutters add stylish practicality. A sliding door leads out to the north-facing deck, perfect for outdoor meals or relaxing with your book.\r\n\r\nThe garden is filled with beautiful planting and enjoys all-day sun, providing space to potter, entertain or simply settle into a favourite chair. With the cricket reserve beyond, you can follow a match or enjoy the activity and open outlook without leaving home.\r\n\r\nThe home offers two bedrooms, one bathroom, a generous-sized laundry with storage, and an internally accessed garage down steps. Currently divided between garden/bicycle/tool storage and an office area with a daybed, the garage offers useful flexibility. The owner says this cosy area is a favourite with the grandchildren when they come for sleepovers.\r\n\r\nThe setting makes everyday life a pleasure. Cheltenham Beach is a short stroll away, with Torpedo Bay in the other direction and North Head close by for exploring. An easy, flat walk along the waterfront takes you past cafés and into Devonport Village, with its shops, eateries and ferry connections to the CBD. A regular bus service across the road adds further convenience.\r\n\r\nThe evening light on Mount Victoria and the distant Sky Tower brings another dimension to this appealing home. Whether you’re watching cricket from the garden, heading to the beach or meeting friends in the village, there is so much to enjoy here.",
